    "https://careers.lincoln.ac.nz/jobdetails/ajid/KDrM7/Scholarships-Programme-Coordinator,2026-25426.html": {
      "title": "Scholarships Programme Coordinator",
      "description": "Scholarships Programme Coordinator -\r\n        Lincoln University Sign in Search jobs Search Show all jobs Keyword or Job Code Locations Any Work type Any Expertise Any show advanced Search careers@lincoln.ac.nz Print Email this job to a friend Apply Apply with Seek Scholarships Programme Coordinator Lead and deliver a dynamic leadership scholarship programme, developing future leaders through coaching, learning experiences, and community impact projects. Mō te tūka | The role As our Scholarships Programme Coordinator, you will lead the delivery, promotion, and ongoing development of the Future Leader Scholarship Programme, creating meaningful opportunities for students to build their leadership capability and contribute to the University and wider community. You'll work closely with scholars, staff, industry partners, and stakeholders to deliver engaging learning experiences, oversee leadership projects, and ensure programme outcomes align with Lincoln University's strategic priorities. Some tasks of the role include: Leading and coordinating the Future Leader Scholarship application and selection process. Designing and delivering leadership workshops, activities, hui, and development opportunities for scholars. Monitoring, evaluating, and reporting on programme performance and outcomes. Building and maintaining relationships with industry, sponsors, professional bodies, and community partners. Overseeing scholar-led projects and providing coaching, mentoring, and guidance to project leaders. Supporting wider scholarship administration activities, including applicant communications, records management, and student enquiries. Mahi & Wāhi / Utu | Work pattern, location & salary This permanent role is based at our Lincoln Campus and works 37.5 hours per week (1.0 FTE). The salary for this position is $80,000 - $85,000 per annum, depending on experience. Kā tino Pūkeka/Whēako | Essential skills/experience for the role To be successful in the role you will have: A relevant tertiary qualification, ideally in adult education, organisational psychology, leadership, or a related field. Experience planning, implementing, and coordinating programmes, ideally within an education, leadership, or development environment. Strong knowledge of leadership principles and experience facilitating learning in adult learning settings. Excellent communication, coaching, and relationship-building skills, with the ability to engage effectively with a wide range of stakeholders. Strong organisational and problem-solving skills, with the ability to manage multiple priorities and adapt to changing needs. High levels of professionalism, integrity, and discretion when working with confidential information. Experience in project management, coaching, or leadership development programmes would be highly regarded. Kā hua ka riro ki a koe | What's in it for you? Join a supportive, inclusive community that values diversity, wellbeing, and professional growth. Benefits include: Flexible, family‑friendly work + free on‑site parking Professional development & mentorship to grow your career Generous leave entitlements – six weeks of paid leave per year (based on 1.0 FTE) Annual salary reviews to recognise your contribution Contributions toward eye tests and prescription eyewear Free, confidential wellbeing support through Clearhead (EAP) Southern Cross employee benefits Access to on‑campus gym with discounted membership On‑site early childhood centre with staff discounts A vibrant campus lifestyle with cafés, green spaces, and a sense of community Mō mātou | About us Te Whare Wānaka o Aoraki | Lincoln University is a specialist institution dedicated to impactful research and higher education that supports land-based industries in New Zealand and globally. Our campus sits at the heart of the Lincoln research precinct, complemented by university-owned farms and research stations that blend education, research, and hands-on learning. At Lincoln, students are at the heart of everything we do, empower them to grow their potential and contribute to a more sustainably productive world through world-class teaching and research. As a progressive university with an ambitious vision, we value a professional workforce that reflects the diversity of our community. Our staff engage with students, parents, government, iwi, and external stakeholders, upholding Lincoln University’s reputation through their work. Our Te Tiriti o Waitangi commitments begin with mana whenua. We honour our special relationship with Ngāi Te Ruahikihiki and Te Taumutu Rūnanga, embedded in our He Tūtohinga Whakamātau | Charter of Understanding. Tono ināianei | Apply now Ready to apply? Submit your CV and a cover letter that highlights your fit - tell us why you want this role and what motivates you to join Lincoln University. Applications received via email will not be considered, however specific enquiry relating to the role can be made to careers@lincoln.ac.nz We are committed to fostering a diverse and inclusive community where everyone feels valued and supported, and we welcome applications from people of all backgrounds. We are only considering applicants who have current unrestricted legal working rights in New Zealand. We are unable to provide visa sponsorship for this role. View the position description at: https://careers.lincoln.ac.nz Job Details Reference # 2026-25426 Posted on 14 Sep 2026 Closes on 30 Sep 2026 18:00 NZST Location(s) Lincoln University Campus Expertise Administration, Project Management Work type(s) Permanent full-time More details (document) PD Scholarships Programme Coordinator September 2026.pdf Print Email this job to a friend Apply Apply with Seek Back © Lincoln University Agency sign in Powered by SnapHire | Privacy policy 8 This site is powered by Snaphire (www.snaphire.com) This site uses Javascript and is required to search and apply for jobs. Your browser either doesn't support Javascript or it is disabled. If you are on a Corporate Network please contact your Administrator for further assistance."
