    "https://careers.lincoln.ac.nz/jobdetails/ajid/1lwM7/Student-Systems-Business-Analyst,2026-25500.html": {
      "title": "Student Systems Business Analyst",
      "description": "Student Systems Business Analyst -\n        Lincoln University Sign in Search jobs Search Show all jobs Keyword or Job Code Locations Any Work type Any Expertise Any show advanced Search careers@lincoln.ac.nz Print Email this job to a friend Apply Apply with Seek Student Systems Business Analyst Drive the performance, improvement and support of the Student Management System, enabling great user experiences and high-quality student data. Mō te tūka | The role As our Student Systems Business Analyst, you'll play a key role in ensuring the University's Student Management System (SMS) is configured, supported, and continuously improved to meet both operational and strategic needs. Acting as the system's subject matter expert, you'll work closely with stakeholders across the University to optimise processes, maintain data integrity, deliver user support and training, and help maximise the value of the system. Some tasks of the role include: Acting as the subject matter expert for the Student Management System, including system configuration, functionality, business rules, and data structures. Monitoring data quality and maintaining the integrity of student information across the system. Identifying and implementing opportunities to improve processes, reporting, user experience, and system utilisation. Testing and validating system enhancements, upgrades, and new functionality to ensure they meet business requirements. Delivering training, support, and guidance to users to build capability and encourage best-practice system use. Collaborating with operational teams, Information Technology staff, and vendors to resolve issues and support ongoing system effectiveness. Based in our Planning and Reporting Office, you'll join a team that provides strategic planning, performance reporting, insights, analysis, and decision support across the University. The team plays an important role in supporting Lincoln University's strategic direction through evidence-based insights, integrated planning, forecasting, and performance monitoring. Mahi & Wāhi / Utu | Work pattern, location & salary This permanent role is based at our Lincoln Campus and works 37.5 hours per week (1.0 FTE). The salary for this position is $85,000 - $90,000 per annum, depending on experience. Kā tino Pūkeka/Whēako | Essential skills/experience for the role To be successful in the role you will have Experience administering, supporting, or configuring a complex business-critical system. Strong problem-solving skills with the ability to analyse, troubleshoot, and resolve system and process issues. Experience planning and conducting system testing, including validating upgrades, enhancements, and new functionality. The ability to identify business improvement opportunities and translate operational requirements into effective system solutions. Excellent communication skills, with the ability to explain technical concepts to a wide range of users. Experience delivering user training and support, along with strong stakeholder relationship management skills. Strong analytical skills and a commitment to maintaining high levels of data accuracy and integrity. Kā hua ka riro ki a koe | What's in it for you? Join a supportive, inclusive community that values diversity, wellbeing, and professional growth. Benefits include: Flexible, family‑friendly work + free on‑site parking Professional development & mentorship to grow your career Generous leave entitlements – six weeks of paid leave per year (based on 1.0 FTE) Annual salary reviews to recognise your contribution Contributions toward eye tests and prescription eyewear Free, confidential wellbeing support through Clearhead (EAP) Southern Cross employee benefits Access to on‑campus gym with discounted membership On‑site early childhood centre with staff discounts A vibrant campus lifestyle with cafés, green spaces, and a sense of community Mō mātou | About us Te Whare Wānaka o Aoraki | Lincoln University is a specialist institution dedicated to impactful research and higher education that supports land-based industries in New Zealand and globally. Our campus sits at the heart of the Lincoln research precinct, complemented by university-owned farms and research stations that blend education, research, and hands-on learning. At Lincoln, students are at the heart of everything we do, empower them to grow their potential and contribute to a more sustainably productive world through world-class teaching and research. As a progressive university with an ambitious vision, we value a professional workforce that reflects the diversity of our community. Our staff engage with students, parents, government, iwi, and external stakeholders, upholding Lincoln University’s reputation through their work. Our Te Tiriti o Waitangi commitments begin with mana whenua. We honour our special relationship with Ngāi Te Ruahikihiki and Te Taumutu Rūnanga, embedded in our He Tūtohinga Whakamātau | Charter of Understanding. Tono ināianei | Apply now Ready to apply? Submit your CV and a cover letter that highlights your fit - tell us why you want this role and what motivates you to join Lincoln University. Applications received via email will not be considered, however specific enquiry relating to the role can be made to careers@lincoln.ac.nz We are committed to fostering a diverse and inclusive community where everyone feels valued and supported, and we welcome applications from people of all backgrounds. We are only considering applicants who have current unrestricted legal working rights in New Zealand. We are unable to provide visa sponsorship for this role. View the position description at: https://careers.lincoln.ac.nz Job Details Reference # 2026-25500 Posted on 09 Sep 2026 Closes on 30 Sep 2026 18:00 NZST Location(s) Lincoln University Campus Expertise Administration Work type(s) Permanent full-time More details (document) PD Student Systems Business Analyst September 2026.pdf Print Email this job to a friend Apply Apply with Seek Back © Lincoln University Agency sign in Powered by SnapHire | Privacy policy 8 This site is powered by Snaphire (www.snaphire.com) This site uses Javascript and is required to search and apply for jobs. Your browser either doesn't support Javascript or it is disabled. If you are on a Corporate Network please contact your Administrator for further assistance. Loading . . ."
    },
    "https://careers.lincoln.ac.nz/jobdetails/ajid/PlrM7/Applications-Team-Leader,2026-25424.html": {
      "title": "Applications Team Leader",
      "description": "Applications Team Leader -\n        Lincoln University Sign in Search jobs Search Show all jobs Keyword or Job Code Locations Any Work type Any Expertise Any show advanced Search careers@lincoln.ac.nz Print Email this job to a friend Apply Apply with Seek Applications Team Leader Lead a team & oversee enterprise applications, driving reliability, continuous improvement, stakeholder engagement, & service excellence. Mō te tūka | The role Join us as an Applications Team Leader based in our Information Technology Services (ITS) team. In this role, you'll lead the University's Applications team, ensuring our enterprise applications are secure, reliable, fit for purpose, and aligned with the needs of teaching, learning, research, and business operations. Working closely with stakeholders, vendors, and technical teams, you'll provide leadership across application support, service delivery, continuous improvement, governance, and team capability development. You'll also play a key role in enhancing services, managing risks, and delivering great outcomes for our university community. Some tasks of the role include: Leading and coaching a high-performing Applications team Providing senior support and escalation for enterprise applications Driving application lifecycle management and continuous improvement initiatives Building strong relationships with stakeholders, vendors, and service partners Managing application governance, risk, security, and compliance activities Supporting upgrades, enhancements, and the successful delivery of new capabilities Mahi & Wāhi / Utu | Work pattern, location & salary This permanent role is based at our Lincoln Campus and works 37.5 hours per week (1.0 FTE). The salary for this position is $110,000 - $125,000 per annum, depending on experience. Kā tino Pūkeka/Whēako | Essential skills/experience for the role To be successful in the role you will have: Significant experience supporting and administering enterprise business applications within a complex environment Strong troubleshooting and problem-solving skills, including application, integration, and data-related issues Experience leading, mentoring, or coordinating technical teams Sound knowledge of application lifecycle management and IT service management practices Proven ability to build effective relationships with stakeholders, end users, vendors, and service providers Relevant Information Technology qualification (or equivalent experience), with strong communication skills and a commitment to continuous improvement and service excellence Kā hua ka riro ki a koe | What's in it for you? Join a supportive, inclusive community that values diversity, wellbeing, and professional growth. Benefits include: Flexible, family‑friendly work + free on‑site parking Professional development & mentorship to grow your career Generous leave entitlements – six weeks of paid leave per year (based on 1.0 FTE) Annual salary reviews to recognise your contribution Contributions toward eye tests and prescription eyewear Free, confidential wellbeing support through Clearhead (EAP) Southern Cross employee benefits Access to on‑campus gym with discounted membership On‑site early childhood centre with staff discounts A vibrant campus lifestyle with cafés, green spaces, and a sense of community Mō mātou | About us Te Whare Wānaka o Aoraki | Lincoln University is a specialist institution dedicated to impactful research and higher education that supports land-based industries in New Zealand and globally. Our campus sits at the heart of the Lincoln research precinct, complemented by university-owned farms and research stations that blend education, research, and hands-on learning. At Lincoln, students are at the heart of everything we do, empower them to grow their potential and contribute to a more sustainably productive world through world-class teaching and research. As a progressive university with an ambitious vision, we value a professional workforce that reflects the diversity of our community. Our staff engage with students, parents, government, iwi, and external stakeholders, upholding Lincoln University’s reputation through their work. Our Te Tiriti o Waitangi commitments begin with mana whenua. We honour our special relationship with Ngāi Te Ruahikihiki and Te Taumutu Rūnanga, embedded in our He Tūtohinga Whakamātau | Charter of Understanding. Tono ināianei | Apply now Ready to apply? Submit your CV and a cover letter that highlights your fit - tell us why you want this role and what motivates you to join Lincoln University. Applications received via email will not be considered, however specific enquiry relating to the role can be made to careers@lincoln.ac.nz We are committed to fostering a diverse and inclusive community where everyone feels valued and supported, and we welcome applications from people of all backgrounds. We are only considering applicants who have current unrestricted legal working rights in New Zealand. We are unable to provide visa sponsorship for this role. View the position description at: https://careers.lincoln.ac.nz Job Details Reference # 2026-25424 Posted on 04 Sep 2026 Closes on 20 Sep 2026 18:00 NZST Location(s) Lincoln University Campus Expertise Information Technology Work type(s) Permanent full-time More details (document) PD Applications Team Leader September 2026.pdf Print Email this job to a friend Apply Apply with Seek Back © Lincoln University Agency sign in Powered by SnapHire | Privacy policy 8 This site is powered by Snaphire (www.snaphire.com) This site uses Javascript and is required to search and apply for jobs. Your browser either doesn't support Javascript or it is disabled. If you are on a Corporate Network please contact your Administrator for further assistance. Loading . . ."
